(1773695, 239368, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Imagineer:</b></div><hr/><i> No offence whatsoever! Thanks for commenting.<br/> <br/>I did question this submission of two though - and could probably have scored higher for the DPC aesthetic if I''d submitted the other<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=242307" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8860/thumb/242307.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8860/thumb/242307.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8860/thumb/242307.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I agree this second one would likely have scored higher; it has a little more ''razzle-dazzle''.  However, I still prefer the actual entry.  For me it better communicates the fleeting, impermanent nature of the commuter''s relationship with his environment.  He''s right there, passing through it, but he''s not really OF it ... he''s in a ''non-place''.  Presumably, the title suggests you were exploring that sort of idea?  What I specifically prefer about the entered image is, as I said in my comments during voting, the fact that the commuter''s attention appears directed at the reflected destination/location (?) sign.  Coupled with the alien-looking light source, this reflected illusion creates a surreal impression that, for the commuter, the journey could as well be intergalactic as intersuburban.  On the other hand, maybe I''ve just been looking at the damned thing for too long?  Either way, it''s entertaining and stimulates thought.</td>', 'Originally posted by Imagineer: No offence whatsoever! Thanks for commenting. I did question this submission of two though - and could probably have scored higher for the DPC aesthetic if I''d submitted the other  I agree this second one would likely have scored higher; it has a little more ''razzle-dazzle''.  However, I still prefer the actual entry.  For me it better communicates the fleeting, impermanent nature of the commuter''s relationship with his environment.  He''s right there, passing through it, but he''s not really OF it ... he''s in a ''non-place''.  Presumably, the title suggests you were exploring that sort of idea?  What I specifically prefer about the entered image is, as I said in my comments during voting, the fact that the commuter''s attention appears directed at the reflected destination/location (?) sign.  Coupled with the alien-looking light source, this reflected illusion creates a surreal impression that, for the commuter, the journey could as well be intergalactic as intersuburban.  On the other hand, maybe I''ve just been looking at the damned thing for too long?  Either way, it''s entertaining and stimulates thought.', '2005-10-10 09:13:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1773699, 238797, 4477, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the blue ribbon Peter!</td>', 'Congrats on the blue ribbon Peter!', '2005-10-10 09:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1773732, 239292, 35357, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kpriest:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow - stunning image, Slippy! Not a bad finish either. Your title probably cost you a few places though. Are you seeing a good shrink? Apparently not. :)<br/> <br/>btw, how often do they change the spark plug at the top of that thing? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, I figured the title would put some folks off, but I couldn''t help myself. :-D  I''ve got the best shrink available, I got his number from the side of a box of Lucky Charms.  I think he''s working wonders! :-P</td>', 'Originally posted by kpriest: Wow - stunning image, Slippy! Not a bad finish either. Your title probably cost you a few places though. Are you seeing a good shrink? Apparently not. :) btw, how often do they change the spark plug at the top of that thing?   Thanks, I figured the title would put some folks off, but I couldn''t help myself. :-D  I''ve got the best shrink available, I got his number from the side of a box of Lucky Charms.  I think he''s working wonders! :-P', '2005-10-10 09:45:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1773736, 239368, 23394, '<td valign="top">i would imagine you were caring about something else far removed from dpc, or commuting for that matter <br/> <br/>;-)</td>', 'i would imagine you were caring about something else far removed from dpc, or commuting for that matter  ;-)', '2005-10-10 09:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1773745, 239420, 11738, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jads:</b></div><hr/><i> I LOVE this photo!  It illustrates that for some people, life is just across the bridge if only they could get to it.  Depression, loneliness, homelessness - Life on the other side. Maybe the chair is empty because the person who sits in it is already on their way to the other side - towards life....or death?  A very evocative shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for leaving such a detailed comment on my photo.  I''m very happy to see that the image can stimulate thought to such an extent.  I just found that the old chair and the bridge in the background made for a good combo.</td>', 'Originally posted by jads: I LOVE this photo!  It illustrates that for some people, life is just across the bridge if only they could get to it.  Depression, loneliness, homelessness - Life on the other side. Maybe the chair is empty because the person who sits in it is already on their way to the other side - towards life....or death?  A very evocative shot!   Thanks for leaving such a detailed comment on my photo.  I''m very happy to see that the image can stimulate thought to such an extent.  I just found that the old chair and the bridge in the background made for a good combo.', '2005-10-10 09:54:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1773746, 237879, 37961, '<td valign="top">Excellent! Wow, 13th place. Won''t be long till your ribboning!</td>', 'Excellent! Wow, 13th place. Won''t be long till your ribboning!', '2005-10-10 09:56:10.000000', NULL, 0),
