(1776474, 238753, 41931, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thehitter:</b></div><hr/><i> that is pretty but since when does the sun rise over the ocean (west) in malibu? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The entire coastline of California runs roughly east/west from Santa Monica to Port Hueneme. There are plenty of small headlands in that stretch where you can actually look east at the water. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>yes, but i surf that beach all the time and have never seen the sun rise over the water. nice shot but it is either sunset or not malibu.</td>', 'Originally posted by bear_music: Originally posted by thehitter: that is pretty but since when does the sun rise over the ocean (west) in malibu?   The entire coastline of California runs roughly east/west from Santa Monica to Port Hueneme. There are plenty of small headlands in that stretch where you can actually look east at the water.  yes, but i surf that beach all the time and have never seen the sun rise over the water. nice shot but it is either sunset or not malibu.', '2005-10-11 13:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
