(1776687, 238753, 17377, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thehitter:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thehitter:</b></div><hr/><i> that is pretty but since when does the sun rise over the ocean (west) in malibu? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The entire coastline of California runs roughly east/west from Santa Monica to Port Hueneme. There are plenty of small headlands in that stretch where you can actually look east at the water. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>yes, but i surf that beach all the time and have never seen the sun rise over the water. nice shot but it is either sunset or not malibu. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The thumb nail below clearly shows how the photo was taken.  "At Sunrise"<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=242318" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17377/thumb/242318.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17377/thumb/242318.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17377/thumb/242318.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by thehitter: Originally posted by bear_music: Originally posted by thehitter: that is pretty but since when does the sun rise over the ocean (west) in malibu?   The entire coastline of California runs roughly east/west from Santa Monica to Port Hueneme. There are plenty of small headlands in that stretch where you can actually look east at the water.  yes, but i surf that beach all the time and have never seen the sun rise over the water. nice shot but it is either sunset or not malibu.   The thumb nail below clearly shows how the photo was taken.  "At Sunrise" ', '2005-10-11 15:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
