(1781640, 238056, 41746, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all of you for being so positive and inspiring in your comments. AS this is my first top 50 photo and the first with 6+ I´m really happy with the results.</td>', 'Thanks to all of you for being so positive and inspiring in your comments. AS this is my first top 50 photo and the first with 6+ I´m really happy with the results.', '2005-10-13 06:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1781946, 239461, 26255, '<td valign="top"><b>**Critique Club**</b> <br/> <br/><b><u>Initial Impression:</u></b>Beautiful Panorama<br/> <br/><b><u>Detailed analysis:</u></b>This is a great panaroma shot.  I love the rich golden colors of the safflower.  Several comments were made on the choice of cropping, but personally I like it.  I''m afraid it may have affected some of the voting because the image can be perceived as being "too small". You did a good job of adhering to the 640 max dimension rule and made the image as large as you could.  I love the flowing curves of the hills and how the sky seems to also "go with the flow".<br/> <br/>My only nitpick would be the blown highlights in the clouds (dead center), but it''s a minor issue that I didn''t even notice in my first pass.<br/> <br/>I also can''t help but wonder what this same image would look like "stretched" vertically.<br/> <br/><b><u>Overall Impression:</u></b>  Great shot, good perspective.  I love it!!!</td>', '**Critique Club**  Initial Impression:Beautiful Panorama Detailed analysis:This is a great panaroma shot.  I love the rich golden colors of the safflower.  Several comments were made on the choice of cropping, but personally I like it.  I''m afraid it may have affected some of the voting because the image can be perceived as being "too small". You did a good job of adhering to the 640 max dimension rule and made the image as large as you could.  I love the flowing curves of the hills and how the sky seems to also "go with the flow". My only nitpick would be the blown highlights in the clouds (dead center), but it''s a minor issue that I didn''t even notice in my first pass. I also can''t help but wonder what this same image would look like "stretched" vertically. Overall Impression:  Great shot, good perspective.  I love it!!!', '2005-10-13 12:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782039, 239515, 12253, '<td valign="top">Beautiful night shot of "my town" (well, I never lived there, but I was born there at Michael Reese--I grew up in Gary, Indiana).  I am mixed about the tilt, I really like the dynamic it adds, but it draws attention to itself too, perhaps because it''s not tilted enough to say: this is purposefully tilted (though I am sure it was).  <br/> <br/>Overall, a great night city scene: hope you have a big version of this hanging on your wall!</td>', 'Beautiful night shot of "my town" (well, I never lived there, but I was born there at Michael Reese--I grew up in Gary, Indiana).  I am mixed about the tilt, I really like the dynamic it adds, but it draws attention to itself too, perhaps because it''s not tilted enough to say: this is purposefully tilted (though I am sure it was).   Overall, a great night city scene: hope you have a big version of this hanging on your wall!', '2005-10-13 13:27:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782141, 238056, 26255, '<td valign="top"><b>**Critique Club**</b> <br/> <br/><b><u>Initial Impression:</u></b>Nice textures.<br/> <br/><b><u>Detailed analysis:</u></b>This is a very pleasant shot.  It gives me a warm, cozy feeling.  I really like the slightly desaturated tones, it really adds to the "rustic" and "charming" feeling of the image.  The door is very bright, and the shadow cast by the chair on the door is minimally distracting.  Maybe a slight burn on the door would help tone it down just a touch.  I also think I would like to see just a tiny bit more cropping out of the left side of the image.  The lighting overall is good as is your composition.  The textures on the wall and table really add to the atmosphere.<br/> <br/><b><u>Overall Impression:</u></b> Nice "warm fuzzy" picture.  Good job!</td>', '**Critique Club**  Initial Impression:Nice textures. Detailed analysis:This is a very pleasant shot.  It gives me a warm, cozy feeling.  I really like the slightly desaturated tones, it really adds to the "rustic" and "charming" feeling of the image.  The door is very bright, and the shadow cast by the chair on the door is minimally distracting.  Maybe a slight burn on the door would help tone it down just a touch.  I also think I would like to see just a tiny bit more cropping out of the left side of the image.  The lighting overall is good as is your composition.  The textures on the wall and table really add to the atmosphere. Overall Impression: Nice "warm fuzzy" picture.  Good job!', '2005-10-13 14:48:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782210, 237349, 31738, '<td valign="top">Good finish but I''m a bit disappointed that this didn''t get a Blue or even make it to the top three because it sure deserves it. Good work.</td>', 'Good finish but I''m a bit disappointed that this didn''t get a Blue or even make it to the top three because it sure deserves it. Good work.', '2005-10-13 15:43:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782906, 239423, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Yep, found Iceland,front and almost center.<br/>:)<br/>I''m afraid you found your answer already about how the voters would respond to your image of the world, and your corner of it.  Aside from voter reaction to your version of the Challenge, I like the image and the idea behind it.  <br/> <br/>It has two purple circles down in the South America area that throw me a bit, and it maybe Neat Image would have eliminated the white reflections in Greenland, but as a whole, this does show a lot of effort and it was a tough problem to solve. <br/> <br/>In composition, I wonder how it would have looked if you had placed the globe in one of the sweet spots in the frame, rather than going for the left placement.  Just a thought.<br/> <br/>The main thing is that you seem to have had fun doing this and you learned from it.  <br/> <br/>I wish you continued success in your DPC Challenge entries.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Yep, found Iceland,front and almost center.:)I''m afraid you found your answer already about how the voters would respond to your image of the world, and your corner of it.  Aside from voter reaction to your version of the Challenge, I like the image and the idea behind it.   It has two purple circles down in the South America area that throw me a bit, and it maybe Neat Image would have eliminated the white reflections in Greenland, but as a whole, this does show a lot of effort and it was a tough problem to solve.  In composition, I wonder how it would have looked if you had placed the globe in one of the sweet spots in the frame, rather than going for the left placement.  Just a thought. The main thing is that you seem to have had fun doing this and you learned from it.   I wish you continued success in your DPC Challenge entries.', '2005-10-13 22:23:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782959, 239403, 39664, '<td valign="top">You live is such an exotic place and I am envious.  Someday, when I retire, I plan to visit "Your Corner of the World" and I will fondly remember this incredible shot and you.<br/> <br/>Thank you for sharing!<br/> <br/>Cheryl</td>', 'You live is such an exotic place and I am envious.  Someday, when I retire, I plan to visit "Your Corner of the World" and I will fondly remember this incredible shot and you. Thank you for sharing! Cheryl', '2005-10-13 23:05:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1782960, 239403, 39664, '<td valign="top">PS: we have the same camera but you are much more skilled than I!<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your finish....well deserved!</td>', 'PS: we have the same camera but you are much more skilled than I! Congratulations on your finish....well deserved!', '2005-10-13 23:06:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783261, 239499, 41802, '<td valign="top">Very interesting corner that you have picked.  This shot defiantly makes the viewer look twice to see what is here, and of course some voters might have just blown on by.   I really do like the original thought.  The coloring seems a little off, I seem to notice it the most in the bottom right corner.  The lighting seems off because of the coloring of the green on the bottom compared to the greens located on the upper part of the image.  I think you have more of an abstract view, which is something I love to see.   Good job!</td>', 'Very interesting corner that you have picked.  This shot defiantly makes the viewer look twice to see what is here, and of course some voters might have just blown on by.   I really do like the original thought.  The coloring seems a little off, I seem to notice it the most in the bottom right corner.  The lighting seems off because of the coloring of the green on the bottom compared to the greens located on the upper part of the image.  I think you have more of an abstract view, which is something I love to see.   Good job!', '2005-10-14 01:08:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783262, 237879, 37779, '<td valign="top">Nice placing and BEAUTIFUL picture! You captured the mood very well!</td>', 'Nice placing and BEAUTIFUL picture! You captured the mood very well!', '2005-10-14 01:08:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783278, 239153, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Wow this is an excellent shot of The flowers.  I would have loved to see the flowers a little more connected to a garden in your corner of the world, but this is just a great shot.  The colors and composition are beautiful.  The background defiantly enhancing the enchanting colors of the flowers. I think you have applied the law of thirds perfectly without over doing it, by including three flowers.  Personally I am not the found of border but I guess it does draw some extra attention into The photo. The lighting is also great.  The only thing I could possibly see would be the stem on the large flower looks like it is moving. Good job.</td>', '*Critique Club* Wow this is an excellent shot of The flowers.  I would have loved to see the flowers a little more connected to a garden in your corner of the world, but this is just a great shot.  The colors and composition are beautiful.  The background defiantly enhancing the enchanting colors of the flowers. I think you have applied the law of thirds perfectly without over doing it, by including three flowers.  Personally I am not the found of border but I guess it does draw some extra attention into The photo. The lighting is also great.  The only thing I could possibly see would be the stem on the large flower looks like it is moving. Good job.', '2005-10-14 01:20:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783292, 238952, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club* <br/> <br/>Wow this is an amazing shot.  The flow of the water is the first thing that grabs my attention.  What an wonderful corner of the world. The overall image is just prefect.  The coloring, lighting and composition are all at the best level possible. A very well deserved top 20.  I think the people at this level are just competing between what the voter likes best in appearance because the quality is so amazing.  I love to see breath taking shots like this.  I wish I had more critiques for you but this just an excellent job!</td>', '*Critique Club*  Wow this is an amazing shot.  The flow of the water is the first thing that grabs my attention.  What an wonderful corner of the world. The overall image is just prefect.  The coloring, lighting and composition are all at the best level possible. A very well deserved top 20.  I think the people at this level are just competing between what the voter likes best in appearance because the quality is so amazing.  I love to see breath taking shots like this.  I wish I had more critiques for you but this just an excellent job!', '2005-10-14 01:33:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783300, 239397, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club* <br/> <br/>This is a great shot.  The colors are so vibrant, excellent time of day.  I love the focus you used on the fence post to give the photo a subject, not just a basic landscape image.    I love the contrast, as well it really help the plants on the right side of the post not get lost into the field.  It almost looks like the plants on both sides of the fence are not the same field but very different areas.  The depth of the right side really grabs my attention when I am able to sit and look at the shot.  I saw the comment about the background being soft, but I don''t know if I would like the image as much if it was too strong, it would take away from the real focus.  This is just a great shot.  I think it was just a hard category with so many landscape to grab viewer attention.</td>', '*Critique Club*  This is a great shot.  The colors are so vibrant, excellent time of day.  I love the focus you used on the fence post to give the photo a subject, not just a basic landscape image.    I love the contrast, as well it really help the plants on the right side of the post not get lost into the field.  It almost looks like the plants on both sides of the fence are not the same field but very different areas.  The depth of the right side really grabs my attention when I am able to sit and look at the shot.  I saw the comment about the background being soft, but I don''t know if I would like the image as much if it was too strong, it would take away from the real focus.  This is just a great shot.  I think it was just a hard category with so many landscape to grab viewer attention.', '2005-10-14 01:40:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783311, 239522, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club* <br/> <br/>Great out of the box.  I really love seeing images that grab your attention or make you think.  I like the approach you took by giving it the title ''Mountain View of Beach &amp; Ocean''  it brings an abstract approach to the contest.  I think in an art class this image would have greatly impressed the teacher.  The shadows across the image are also interesting, I don''t think the shot would have worked as well with no shadows.  I think I would have to agree with other in the sandals being my favorite part.  I think the shoes express the title to the fullest extent.  The only small thing I could see it the image seems little soft, maybe a tiny bit more focus.  I would not sharpen the image. Its hard to tell if there is noise in the right hand side of the tile or if it is the tiles themselves.  Good job.</td>', '*Critique Club*  Great out of the box.  I really love seeing images that grab your attention or make you think.  I like the approach you took by giving it the title ''Mountain View of Beach & Ocean''  it brings an abstract approach to the contest.  I think in an art class this image would have greatly impressed the teacher.  The shadows across the image are also interesting, I don''t think the shot would have worked as well with no shadows.  I think I would have to agree with other in the sandals being my favorite part.  I think the shoes express the title to the fullest extent.  The only small thing I could see it the image seems little soft, maybe a tiny bit more focus.  I would not sharpen the image. Its hard to tell if there is noise in the right hand side of the tile or if it is the tiles themselves.  Good job.', '2005-10-14 01:48:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783321, 239537, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club* <br/> <br/>''Life as a Painter''  a great expression of your corner of the world.  I like that you took a piece of yourself and not just the location.  This is a nice tight image.  The coloring and lighting are extremely appealing.  The only I can''t figure out is what you are painting, it almost looks like you are painting paint.  That could just be how naive I am because I have no painting experience.  I bet this image grabbed voter when they were glancing through the thumbnails and they saw this bright red image.  I glanced through your other work and I think you are defiantly talented and will continue to grab people with your strong colors and images.  Good job.</td>', '*Critique Club*  ''Life as a Painter''  a great expression of your corner of the world.  I like that you took a piece of yourself and not just the location.  This is a nice tight image.  The coloring and lighting are extremely appealing.  The only I can''t figure out is what you are painting, it almost looks like you are painting paint.  That could just be how naive I am because I have no painting experience.  I bet this image grabbed voter when they were glancing through the thumbnails and they saw this bright red image.  I glanced through your other work and I think you are defiantly talented and will continue to grab people with your strong colors and images.  Good job.', '2005-10-14 01:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1783431, 238797, 45600, '<td valign="top">great shot mate!  im only 13 but I know talent when I see it!!!!</td>', 'great shot mate!  im only 13 but I know talent when I see it!!!!', '2005-10-14 04:22:48.000000', NULL, 0),
